# Temporal integrity
- Default to confirmed-bar decisions for historical/live consistency.
- Treat higher-timeframe data as unsafe until timing, gaps, and lookahead are reviewed.
- Never use future information, negative plot offsets to imply earlier knowledge, or unconfirmed pivots as confirmed signals.
- Classify each possible repaint source and document accepted real-time variability.
- Require explicit evidence before labeling a script non-repainting.
